    {
      "etag": "\"7da24de31f312ea51aeea55c327ff1e5\"",
      "id": "https://geniza.princeton.edu/annotations/855796e6-8885-4a9d-8945-1f52dcdf7b15/",
      "type": "Annotation",
      "created": "2026-11-12T21:11:30.507733+00:00",
      "modified": "2026-11-12T21:11:30.507744+00:00",
      "dc:source": "https://geniza.princeton.edu/sources/170/",
      "target": {
        "source": {
          "id": "https://iiif.nli.org.il/IIIFv21/FL160305047",
          "type": "Canvas",
          "partOf": {
            "id": "https://geniza.princeton.edu/documents/6552/iiif/manifest/"
          }
        },
        "selector": {
          "type": "FragmentSelector",
          "value": "xywh=pixel:778.154052734375,1869.1688232421875,4028.846923828125,3742.6514892578125",
          "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/"
        }
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Verso",
          "value": "<p>My master, the elder Ab\u016b Sa\u02bfd, informed me that the elder Abu \u2019l-Bishr (\"Good tidings\") sold his silk (\u1e25ar\u012br) to the government and received its price. However, I was in no mood today to ask him how he sold it. I shall sell what I have with me, for I do not see that there is much hope (for a better price).</p>\n<p>My lord, the elder Ab\u016b Sa\u02bfd talked to me about the textiles, namely, which of them had not been sent and had been left with him. I understood that he wanted to get rid of them; so I said perhaps he could find someone to send them with and get them out of his sight.</p>\n<p>My lord, I left my cotton robe, which I used to wear above my iridescent robe; in its pocket there is the tax certificate together with a paper bag in which there are some dirhems and a letter given to me by Sal\u0101ma, the agent of our master, the Nagid\u2014(may his) R(ock) p(reserve him). Please send me the tax certificate as soon as you have read this letter, for I have given a bail bond on it until it arrives.</p>\n<p>Whatever needs you have, please write me about them. Please write me in detail about the price of oil at your place and how things are, for I am very much worried. May God let me receive good tidings, as is his bountiful custom.</p>\n<p>Accept my best greetings, and likewise, my best greetings to the elder Abu \u2019l-\u1e24asan; if he needs anything, let him write me about it. Greetings to Rachel and her mother and to everyone in the house. Greetings also to Abu \u2019l-\u1e24asan, to the son of my paternal aunt, and his sons. And Peace. And may your life be prolonged!</p>\n<p>And look for the storax for me, for I did not find it in the package.</p>",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
